# ChineseListener — Core Agent Rules

## Mission

Work on the **`:app`** Android module as one product. Follow the **docs bundle** from `docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md` and layered practices in `docs/ANDROID_PRACTICES.md`. Prefer cohesive changes over local patches that ignore package boundaries or power impact.

## Human approval (mandatory)

Before **implementing** non-trivial work, stop and get explicit user approval in chat:

- Multi-file or cross-layer changes (ui ↔ presentation ↔ domain ↔ data)
- New or upgraded dependencies, AGP/Kotlin/Compose version bumps, CI changes
- `minSdk` / `targetSdk` / manifest / permission changes
- New modules or architectural splits

**Required in chat first:** problem statement, root-cause hypothesis (with evidence), proposed approach, files/packages touched, risks, and how success will be verified (Gradle tasks, unit tests, device/emulator).

**Do not** edit code until the user approves. Exceptions: single obvious fixes the user fully specified (e.g. “set minSdk to 28”, “go ahead”).

## Root cause and proven fixes

1. **Reproduce and locate** — read code, Gradle files, logs, and tests; trace UI → presentation → domain → data.
2. **Identify root cause** — distinguish symptom from cause; cite evidence.
3. **Fix the cause** — smallest correct change; no speculative refactors with bugfixes.
4. **Verify** — run relevant Gradle tasks; report what was not verified.

## Do not lie (honesty)

- Never fabricate command output, test results, or file contents.
- Never claim verification without running checks in this session when feasible.
- Label guesses as unverified.

## Single source of truth

| Topic | Source of truth |
|--------|------------------|
| APIs, packages, UI | Repo `*.kt`, `AndroidManifest.xml`, `build.gradle.kts` |
| Versions | Root `build.gradle.kts` and `app/build.gradle.kts` — do not invent dependency versions |
| Android API levels | `minSdk`, `targetSdk`, `compileSdk` in `app/build.gradle.kts` |
| Kotlin / Android | [Kotlin docs](https://kotlinlang.org/docs/home.html), [Jetpack Compose](https://developer.android.com/jetpack/compose) |
| Project docs | **`docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md` is the bundle entry** — `@docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md` means read **all** bundle files listed there (see `chinese-listener-docs-bundle.mdc`) |

## Engineering principles

- **SOLID**, **DRY**, **KISS**, **YAGNI**
- **Strict layering** — see `chinese-listener-architecture.mdc` and `docs/ANDROID_PRACTICES.md` (ui → presentation → domain ← data)
- **Idiomatic Kotlin** — multi-paradigm: `data class`/`sealed`, immutability, coroutines/Flow, no `GlobalScope`; **same refactor/collection approach as kotlin-mutliplatform-test** (see `chinese-listener-code-style.mdc`, `chinese-listener-kotlin-collections.mdc`, `docs/CODE_AND_REFACTOR_STYLE.md`)

## Quality bar

- **`test`** (unit) required for domain/presentation logic; **instrumented tests** when Android adapters change
- **UDF:** explicit `UiState` / events; no business logic in composables
- No secrets in repo (`local.properties` is local-only)
- Accessibility and lifecycle-aware Compose where UI changes matter
- **Energy efficiency:** lifecycle-scoped coroutines, no default polling; see `chinese-listener-energy-efficiency.mdc`
- External guidance: [Android app architecture](https://developer.android.com/topic/architecture), [Kotlin coding conventions](https://kotlinlang.org/docs/coding-conventions.html)

## Git (read-only analysis; no push)

**Never push.** Allowed: `status`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `blame`. No commit/merge/rebase unless the user explicitly asks in that conversation.

## Communication and citations (mandatory in chat)

| Claim type | Citation |
|------------|----------|
| Project code/config | `startLine:endLine:path` from files read this session |
| External docs | Full `https://...` URL |
